      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "A 34-year-old male presented with right sided chest pain, shortness of breath and a swelling over his left foot. Chest radiology revealed a mass lesion in the right middle lobe which on CT guided biopsy showed features of spindle cell sarcoma. Surgical excision of both the lung and foot masses were done, both of which on histopathological examination proved to be spindle cell sarcoma."},
